{"id": "EUVD-2026-82068", "enisaUuid": "f84f47b6-6e92-398c-b42e-1a5afd04fc80", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath11k: fix overreads in ath11k_wmi_process_csa_switch_count_event()\n\nThere is no policy entry for WMI_TAG_PDEV_CSA_SWITCH_COUNT_STATUS_EVENT, so\nthe parse infrastructure does not enforce a minimum length for the event\nstruct. Additionally, the num_vdevs field is taken directly from firmware\nand used as a loop bound over the vdev_ids array without checking that it\nfits within the TLV payload. Either condition can cause an out-of-bounds\nread.\n\nAdd a TLV policy entry for WMI_TAG_PDEV_CSA_SWITCH_COUNT_STATUS_EVENT so\nthe parse infrastructure enforces a minimum length for the fixed-size event\nstruct. Add a helper ath11k_wmi_tlv_data_len() to recover the payload\nlength of a parsed TLV from the header preceding its data pointer. Use it\nin ath11k_wmi_process_csa_switch_count_event() to bound num_vdevs before\nthe loop.\n\nCompile tested only.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:11", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f760b7d7e43584d2fa9bffcec1a04e502609f827", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d6625dc5f1fe42cd81b8c57a1f5317afb9b410ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0364926fb4bfb5b798e5fe2785b3023b4f767327", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5de2b8c53714ad58f2fda118cd29ebbe31b38665", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/208d7fdb85976a737a715b81d54efaff6703880c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hhm8-7qmw-pmj8", "CVE-2026-90407"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1fc33f71-be40-3a0d-bf78-a68a321638de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "30f173a3-74a0-317b-bb9e-41ab4cbdba96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5c65159f2895379e11ca13f62feabe93278985d <d6625dc5f1fe42cd81b8c57a1f5317afb9b410ce"}, {"id": "4de40d7f-c9ee-34e9-9608-f01a3b018ef6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6688b940-3541-3fcd-9b37-3fd4a4e703b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5c65159f2895379e11ca13f62feabe93278985d <f760b7d7e43584d2fa9bffcec1a04e502609f827"}, {"id": "81d8836c-1dbf-3f67-a83e-2883f54b68db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "88c3482f-9f7a-3b31-bc8d-540dcc3b95ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5c65159f2895379e11ca13f62feabe93278985d <5de2b8c53714ad58f2fda118cd29ebbe31b38665"}, {"id": "892e0b76-4d00-333a-918e-e66ed66727e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "98016f96-740e-38cd-b8f1-cd0283004671", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c061e672-f316-3384-be8f-cd69a347e2f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "e2961c66-e311-3ea8-909a-1a3c4e9a7c3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "e6de76e8-d09b-3121-ac0c-0bccdcb17f22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5c65159f2895379e11ca13f62feabe93278985d <208d7fdb85976a737a715b81d54efaff6703880c"}, {"id": "f952e5ef-c26d-3e91-8615-793be183e22f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5c65159f2895379e11ca13f62feabe93278985d <0364926fb4bfb5b798e5fe2785b3023b4f767327"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "55cc3253-c8c7-3c44-957c-e2dcd726c244", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}